# Preventing SQL Injection (SQLi)

**SQL Injection** occurs when untrusted user input is directly concatenated into a SQL statement string, allowing attackers to execute unauthorized commands.

---

## Prevention: Parameterized Queries & ORMs

```typescript
// ❌ VULNERABLE: Direct string concatenation
const query = `SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '${req.body.email}'`;

// ✅ SECURE: Parameterized Query (Prepared Statement)
const query = 'SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = $1';
const result = await db.query(query, [req.body.email]);
```

> **Rule:** Parameterized queries treat user input strictly as **literal data**, never as executable SQL tokens.
